    <span id="page-body"></span>
    <div id="maincontent3" class="article" role="main"> <!-- InstanceBeginEditable name="maincontent2" -->
      <h1>Bureau of Labor Standards</h1>
      <p>The Bureau of Labor Standards helps workers and businesses make their worksites safer; upholds standards for minimum wages, child labor and other practices; and gathers information on the rapidly changing world of work in Maine today - and in the future.</p>
      <div class="rounded box">
        <table border="0">
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><p></p>
                <button class="accordion"><strong>Labor Laws</strong></button>
                <div class="panel">
                  <ul type="disc">
                    <li><a href="../labor_laws/mma/index.shtml" target="_blank">Maine Monitor Advocate</a></li>
                    <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/earnedpaidleave/" target="_blank">Earned Paid Leave Information</a></li>
                    <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/cleanenergy/" target="_blank">Energy Facility Construction</a></li>
                    <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/wagehour.shtml">Summary of Labor Laws</a>&nbsp;(includes minimum wage, overtime, independent contractor, and other laws)</li>
                    <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/minorsguide/">Child Labor Laws and Child Labor Rules</a></li>
                    <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/substanceusetesting/">Substance Use Testing Law</a></li>
                    <li><a href="http://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_stats/publications/wagerateconst/index.html">Prevailing Wage Certification for State Funded Construction Projects</a></li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <p></p>
                <button class="accordion"><strong>Workplace Safety and Health</strong></button>
                <div class="panel">
                  <ul>
                    <li><a href="http://www.safetyworksmaine.com/">SafetyWorks!</a>&nbsp;(Includes workplace safety training classes and consultations)</li>
                    <li><a href="http://maine.gov/labor/labor_stats/research.html">Safety Research</a></li>
                    <li><a href="http://maine.gov/labor/posters/index.html">Free Labor Posters</a></li>
                    <li><a href="http://maine.gov/labor/workplace_safety/publicsector.shtml">Public Sector Safety Enforcement</a></li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <p></p>
                <button class="accordion"><strong>Workplace Statistics</strong></button>
                <div class="panel">
                  <ul>
                    <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/bls/researchstats/" target="_blank">Research and Statistics Division</a>&nbsp;(Provides data and analysis relating to workplace injuries, illnesses etc.)</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <p></p>
                <button class="accordion"><strong>Posters and Forms</strong></button>
                <div class="panel">
                  <ul>
                    <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/docs/2019/bls/MaineCertifiedPayrollFormrev10042019.pdf" target="_blank">Download Certified Payroll Form</a> (PDF)</li>
                    <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/labor_laws/publications/2018/work_permit_072018.pdf" target="_blank">Download the Work Permit Application</a> (PDF)</li>
                    <li><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/posters/index.shtml" target="_blank">Free Labor Posters</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/labor/docs/2022/laborlaws/LaborResourcesforSingleWorkingWomensWeek.pdf" target="_blank">Labor Resources for Parents</a> (PDF)</li>
                    <li><a href="http://maine.gov/labor/labor_stats/data_profiles.html">Request an Injury Data Profile for Your Business</a></li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <p></p>
				  <button class="accordion"><strong>Wage and Hour Violations</strong></button>
                <div class="panel">
                  <p><a href="https://www.maine.gov/labor/bls/whv/" target="_blank">Wage and Hour Violations</a></p>
                </div>
                <p></p>
				<button class="accordion"><strong>Wage and Hour  Classes and  Webinars</strong></button>
                <div class="panel">
                  <p><strong>In-person Wage and Hour Classes </strong><br>
                    <br>
                  <a href="https://safetyworksmaine.gov/training/scheduled-classes" target="_blank">Browse the schedule and register here</a>. </p>
                  <p><strong><br>
                    Tuesday Topics Webinar Series for Employers</strong><br>
                </p>
                  <p>Have questions about Maine's labor laws and workplace requirements? Join the Maine Department of Labor for Tuesday Topics, a monthly webinar series designed to help employers understand Maine's labor laws and workplace requirements. Each session covers a different topic and provides practical information and resources to help employers meet their responsibilities and support their employees.</p>
                  <p>Tuesday Topics webinars are offered in two live Zoom sessions on the same day, at 10 a.m. and 1:30 p.m. Registration is not required; simply select a topic below to learn more about the session and join.</p>
                  <p>The Maine Department of Labor provides equal opportunity in employment and programs. Auxiliary aids and services are available to people with disabilities upon request by contacting Tina Duffany at 207-623-7912 or <a href="mailto:Tina.Duffany@maine.gov?subject=BLS%20Tuesday%20Topic%20question" target="_blank">Tina.Duffany@maine.gov</a>.</p>
					
				  <div><h4></h4>

<p></p>
